<title>USA: Mid-America Bancorp Q3 shr rises to $0.38.</title>
<headline>Mid-America Bancorp Q3 shr rises to $0.38.</headline>
<dateline>LOUISVILLE, Ky. 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr	profit $0.38	    loss  $0.16</p>
<p> Net	profit 3,478	    loss  1,476</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  9,205		    n/a</p>
<p>	  Nine months</p>
<p> Shr	profit $1.25	    profit$0.50</p>
<p> Net	profit 11,502	   profit4,555</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  9,212		    9,192</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: Per share data for 1995 has adjusted for 3 percent stock dividend declared November 20, 1995.</p>
<p>1996 Net income for the quarter and nine months increased significantly over comparable 1995 periods in part because of loan losses, interest reversals and expenses related to non-performing real estate development loans to one borrower that reduced net income for the 1995 periods by about $4.9 million.</p>
</text>
